+# Cancelling a Booked Visit Stays Out of Scope; Correcting One Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 declined both changing and cancelling a visit once booked. The owner confirmed that row as deliberate on 2026-08-08, in [the deletion and visit-amendment ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md). That ADR states that narrowing the row later is a recorded owner decision with its own non-goal ADR.
+
+On 2026-11-05 the owner requested visit editing and decided the row at intake: "Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-5 whole.** Rejected by the owner's decision.
+2. **Remove NG-5.** Rejected: the owner keeps cancellation out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-5 now declines cancelling a booked visit and nothing else. Correcting a booked visit's date and description is in scope, as [`REQ-VIS-003`](../prd.md#req-vis-003). The 2026-08-08 decision on NG-4 is unchanged.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A booked visit is no longer immutable: its date and description can be corrected. Its pet cannot change.
+- Cancellation stays declined. A cancelled visit would add lifecycle state the sample carries nowhere else.
+- The owner detail page gains no edit link in this change; the owner named a visible entry point as a possible follow-up request.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed NG-5 row.
+- [PRD Visits](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the correction requirement.
